{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1530644-correspondence-special-rules","id":1530644,"title":"Correspondence Special Rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-12T08:22:42-08:00","id":1530644,"title":"Correspondence Special Rules","content":"Most of the Spheres have some extra rules that apply to only them, from Forces having size limitations by rank to Spirit and Mind having special difficulty rules. Many of them I understand. They're not particularly graceful but they work towards an understandable goal. Correspondence, though, has two that are making me scratch my head.<br /> <br /> 1) In conjunctional effects that involve Correspondence, the other spheres are capped at the mage's Correspondence Rank. A mage with Correspondence 2 cannot cast a Forces 3/Correspondence 2 spell. I understand this as a limit for casting at a distance, and I actually thought that was the rule until recently, but as written this applies to all Correspondence uses. A mage with Correspondence 1 cannot incorporate spatial perceptions with other higher ranked spheres.<br /> <br /> 2) Making permanent gates, for some reason, takes 10 or more successes rather than the 6+ for everything else. Considering the actual amount of successes is ST discretion both ways, I really don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Possibly these are game balance issues, but I haven't had to deal with players abusing gates, wards, or spatial perception. Has anyone else?<br /> <br /> For that matter, has anyone run across abuse of Time where they wish it had similar rules to Correspondence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T19:49:49-07:00","id":1536127,"title":"","content":"I had the same interpretation as you for the first, and I will keep it. The second... I can imagine a group abusing portal creation, but it is largely theoretical and I don't think raising the success cost would change it a lot.<br /> <br /> Maybe they envisioned someone applying too much extra effects to the portal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T13:24:51-07:00","id":1536166,"title":"","content":"Theoreticaly a open portal to someones back or head where you can stab or shoot could be abusable. But that requires pattern locking and would require a lot of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T16:48:01-07:00","id":1536172,"title":"","content":"An open portal to someone's back or head would actually be a ridiculously unnecessarily hard way to hurt someone. It's like killing a person with a bomb that only explodes if inserted in the middle of the brain with a 12 gauge shotgun modified to do no damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T01:51:59-07:00","id":1536612,"title":"","content":"I believe that the first limitation is a miscommunication of how correspondence functions.<br /> <br /> the limitation on conjunctional effects has only applied to when making use of the correspondence ranges table. I.e. if you want to transform something in the next room over or targeting a specific person on the other side of the world. If you just want to make a wonder that grants Corr1 360 vision, you do not need Corr 4 because you need Prime 4 to make said wonder, Corr 1 is fine. Similarly there are many examples of rotes where corr is not the higher ranked sphere, but said rotes make use of correspondence\u2019s purview that does not require the range table, such as sensing the strength of connection between two objects or people in the room, or setting up a ward.<br /> <br /> ignore what HDYDT says about this not being the case, there are rotes in M20 which contradict this.<br /> <br /> <br /> as for wards, this is more a general point on magic. The default is that all magic which creates or transmutes is impermanent without quintessence and investment of power (successes).<br /> <br /> the exact number of successes required for permanence has always been in flux. Some have it that without Prime 2 to make thing a trinket like wonder, true permanence is quite simply impossible. The best you can get is indefinet duration which will be eroded by unbelief. This isn\u2019t a specific facet of correspondence wards and portals though, it\u2019s all magic which create fundamental consensus breaking effects long term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}